# App
CONFIG_DIR=config/
OPENAI_API_KEY=...
DB_HOST=localhost
DB_PORT=5432
DB_USER=postgres
DB_PASSWORD=postgres
DB_NAME=nativespeaker

# Tests (e2e)
# JWT_API_KEY, not FIREBASE_API_KEY: pydantic-settings maps it onto `jwt.api_key`
# through the nested delimiter, and the old name is now merely an ignored extra key.
JWT_PROJECT_ID=...
JWT_API_KEY=...
FIREBASE_TEST_EMAIL=...
FIREBASE_TEST_PASSWORD=...

# --- Firebase Admin credential: EITHER of the two below, tried in this order ---
#
# Both end in the same named Admin app, and everything except completion mode runs
# with neither: the service boots, prepare mode works, and a real completion fails
# closed as 503 verification_temporarily_unavailable. The e2e real-anonymous case
# (tests/e2e/test_create_user.py::TestTheRealAnonymousCompletion) SKIPS -- it does
# not fail -- when neither is present, naming both in the skip reason.
#
# 1. Application Default Credentials (preferred, and the only route on projects
#    whose org policy sets iam.disableServiceAccountKeyCreation -- as this one
#    does, so no service-account key can be minted here at all). Point it at an
#    ADC file kept OUTSIDE the repo, mode 600, or use a `gcloud auth
#    application-default login` session. Google's own guidance ranks this above
#    key files, which "are a security risk if not managed correctly".
GOOGLE_APPLICATION_CREDENTIALS=/absolute/path/outside/this/repo/application_default_credentials.json
#
# 2. An explicit service-account key (D-08): the whole JSON on ONE line, from the
#    Firebase console (Project settings -> Service accounts -> Generate new
#    private key). Used in preference to ADC when set.
# NEVER commit the real value -- it belongs in the gitignored .env, and never in
# config/config.yaml, which is tracked and would silently outrank this variable.
FIREBASE_SERVICE_ACCOUNT_JSON={"type":"service_account","project_id":"...","private_key_id":"...","private_key":"...","client_email":"...","client_id":"...","token_uri":"https://oauth2.googleapis.com/token"}
